# Voice-Controlled Home Automation System Using ESP32 and Google Assistant

## Abstract

This project presents a Voice-Controlled Home Automation System using ESP32, Google Assistant, and Sinric Pro. The system enables users to control connected devices using voice commands. Google Assistant processes voice commands and communicates with Sinric Pro Cloud, which forwards the commands to the ESP32 through a Wi-Fi network. In this implementation, three LEDs (Red, Green, and Blue) are used to represent smart appliances. The system demonstrates real-time wireless control and provides a low-cost solution for smart home automation.

---

## Introduction

Voice-controlled systems have become an important component of modern smart homes. With the advancement of Internet of Things (IoT) technology, users can interact with devices using natural language commands through voice assistants.

This project demonstrates a voice-controlled home automation system using ESP32 and Google Assistant. Sinric Pro acts as the cloud platform that connects Google Assistant with the ESP32. Voice commands are used to control multiple devices represented by LEDs.

