## Methodology

The ESP32 is connected to a Wi-Fi network and authenticated using Sinric Pro credentials. Three virtual devices are configured on the Sinric Pro dashboard. Google Assistant is linked with Sinric Pro to enable voice control.

When a voice command is issued, Google Assistant sends the command to Sinric Pro Cloud. Sinric Pro forwards the command to the ESP32, which controls the corresponding GPIO pin and changes the state of the associated LED.

---

## Working Principle

1. ESP32 connects to the Wi-Fi network.
2. Sinric Pro authenticates the ESP32 device.
3. Google Assistant receives a voice command.
4. The command is transmitted to Sinric Pro Cloud.
5. Sinric Pro forwards the command to ESP32.
6. ESP32 controls the corresponding GPIO output.
7. The selected LED turns ON or OFF.

